#+TITLE: cl-charms backend .asd: secondary system name is unloadable
#+STATUS: TODO
#+PRIORITY: P3

* Symptom

The documented load workflow for the optional ncurses backend fails:

: (asdf:load-asd #p".../autolisp-debug-ui-tui-charms/clautolisp-charms.asd")
: (asdf:load-system "clautolisp/autolisp-debug-ui-tui-charms")
: => Component "clautolisp-charms" not found

* Cause

=clautolisp/autolisp-debug-ui-tui-charms/clautolisp-charms.asd= defines the
system *clautolisp/autolisp-debug-ui-tui-charms*. That is a SECONDARY system
whose primary name is =clautolisp=, so ASDF expects it in =clautolisp.asd=
(the aggregate) — not in a file named =clautolisp-charms.asd=. ASDF's
find-system for the secondary re-searches the =clautolisp= primary (the
aggregate), which does not define it, and fails. The .asd's own header
documents the broken workflow as if it worked.

This backend is INTENTIONALLY outside the aggregate (it needs cl-charms /
libncurses + a real terminal, must never be a build/CI dependency); the
problem is only its ASDF *name*, not its exclusion.

* Fix options

1. Rename the system to a standalone primary matching the file:
   =(defsystem "clautolisp-charms" …)= in =clautolisp-charms.asd=, then
   =(asdf:load-system "clautolisp-charms")= works once the .asd is on the
   registry (or after an explicit load-asd). Update the two doc references
   (=documentation/clautolisp-debugger-{design-notes,ui-implementation-plan}.org=)
   and the .asd header example.
2. Or rename the file to =clautolisp.asd='s directory convention — not viable
   (would collide with the aggregate).

Option 1 is the intended fix.

* Not blocking the CLI

=clautolisp --debugger-ui ncurses= no longer depends on this: NCURSES-TERMINAL-SCREEN
(tools/clautolisp/source/main.lisp) resolves the backend by find-package /
find-symbol on =clautolisp.ui.tui.charms= — it uses the backend when already
loaded into the image and otherwise warns and falls back to the tui UI. This
ticket is about making the *documented explicit load* work, so the backend can
be loaded (from an init file or a charms-including build) in the first place.

* Related

Surfaced while wiring =--debugger-ui ncurses= to a real terminal screen
(debugger-ui-ncurses-aldb branch): before this, selecting ncurses crashed with
an unbound SCREEN slot because nothing ever built a charms-screen for it.
